     "summary": "A free introductory finance textbook from OpenStax (Rice University). Its chapters on the time value of money explain present value, future value, annuities and net present value with worked examples; its chapters on returns and the historical performance of US markets explain simple and compound returns, average returns and standard deviation as a measure of risk; its statistics and regression chapters cover means, spread, the normal distribution, correlation and fitting a regression line in finance settings; and its chapter on investing explains diversification, beta and the capital asset pricing model at an introductory level. It is a good first read for the plain-words version of ideas 1, 5, 6, 7, 10, 11, 13, 14 and 20. Licence note: the book is released under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0, which does not allow commercial use, so this library keeps only this description and the link; read the book itself at the link. Caveat: it is an introductory text and does not cover the quantitative models (GARCH, Kalman filtering, market making) the rest of this library explains."}
